# UI Patterns (shadcn/ui + Tailwind v4)

## Component Structure
- All shadcn/ui components live in `src/components/ui/`
- Domain components organized by surface: `admin/`, `public/`, `portal/`, `shared/`
- Each domain component is a single file unless it exceeds ~200 lines, then split

## List Pages Pattern
```tsx
export function ContactsList() {
  const contacts = useQuery(api.contacts.queries.list, { orgId });
  if (!contacts) return <TableSkeleton columns={5} rows={10} />;
  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
        <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Contacts</h1>
        <Button onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>Add Contact</Button>
      </div>
      <DataTable columns={columns} data={contacts} searchKey="company" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Form Dialog Pattern
```tsx
<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
  <DialogContent>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>{editing ? "Edit" : "New"} Contact</DialogTitle>
    </DialogHeader>
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="space-y-4">
        <FormField control={form.control} name="company"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Company</FormLabel>
              <FormControl><Input {...field} /></FormControl>
              <FormMessage />
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        <DialogFooter>
          <Button type="submit" disabled={isPending}>Save</Button>
        </DialogFooter>
      </form>
    </Form>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Data Table (TanStack Table)
- Create a reusable `DataTable` component wrapping TanStack Table
- Column definitions per entity in the same file as the list component
- Features: sorting, filtering, pagination, row selection
- Search input filters the primary text column

## Loading States
- Use `Skeleton` for initial data loads
- Use `Button` disabled state with spinner for mutations
- Use `Suspense` boundaries at route segment level

## Responsive Design
- Admin sidebar: collapsible on mobile via `Sheet` component
- Tables: horizontal scroll on mobile
- Forms: single column on mobile, two columns on desktop for address/telecom fields
- Use Tailwind responsive prefixes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`
